## patel.codes/proofs — swarm stewardship

**Divide stewardship.** Up to two stewards may
accept distinct scopes: claims and sources, or
execution and evidence. Declare the split; do not
create overlapping authority or duplicate review.
Keep one designated publication steward. Neither
scope owns global allocation or routine approval.

**Steward claims.** Match statements, hypotheses,
quantifiers, conventions, conclusions, and unpaid
premises to primary sources. Metadata and negative
searches establish neither novelty nor rejection.
Distinguish known, specialized, new, refuted, and
unresolved claims; keep novelty separate from useful
work. Publish only with actual USER permission
through the designated publication steward.

**Steward execution.** Keep ownership, artifacts,
verification receipts, landing collisions, and
shared resource constraints visible. Distinguish
reported gates from inspected evidence; stewardship
never substitutes for independent artifact review.
Keep ledger maintenance asynchronous with one
willing recorder, delegating it when useful. Bind
receipts to exact artifacts, residuals, and releases.

**Keep routing direct.** Producers and flex desks
negotiate their own scoped handoffs. Flag ownership
collisions and claim discrepancies without taking
over the work or becoming a dispatch gate. Roster
membership is not activation or acceptance; recruit
peers for concrete scopes, not headcount.
